{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"For an Irish UCITS ETF **or ETF share class**, distinguish:\n\n- **Transparency-policy disclosures:** The 2026 regulations require disclosure of the portfolio-transparency policy and where portfolio information is available, alongside applicable indicative-NAV information. Disclosing a policy is not itself publishing holdings.\n- **Daily public holdings:** Publishing the full portfolio publicly every day is one transparency approach—not an unconditional requirement for every ETF.\n- **Conditional periodic route:** CBI Q&A 1012 (April 2025) permits periodic public holdings disclosure, subject to its conditions, including daily provision to authorised participants/market makers of information sufficient for effective arbitrage. That daily information channel is distinct from daily public publication; it should not automatically be described as requiring identical full-holdings disclosure to everyone.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Neither a transparency-policy statement nor daily AP/market-maker information alone establishes that the conditions for periodic public disclosure have been met."}}
